# ── Compose substitution vars (PUBLIC — no secrets belong in this file) ──

# Pin the image by DIGEST for immutability (not a moving tag). Get the digest:
#   docker buildx imagetools inspect mornedhels/enshrouded-server:1.8.1-proton
# then paste the sha256 below. The audit workflow FAILS if this isn't a digest.
#
# Keen Games publishes no official server image, so this is a community one,
# like every other game here.
#
# The image's PROTON build of release 1.8.1 (2026-10-23), tag `1.8.1-proton`.
# Digest taken from Docker Hub on 2026-11-13. It replaces `dev-proton` from
# 2026-10-15, the development build that first ran Enshrouded 1.0 under Proton.
# 1.8.1 fixes two bugs reported against that line (upstream issues #260, #262),
# both in what this server relies on:
#   - the player count always read "empty" (the a2s library did not load on
#     Python 3.14), so updates - and restarts - could drop players;
#   - an update could restart the server on the OLD build while reporting
#     success, which locks out updated clients ("server version too old").
# Checked on this server on 2026-11-13: dev-proton runs Python 3.14.4 and its
# a2s library fails to import (KeyError: '__annotations__') - bug #260, which
# makes the "only when nobody is online" check count the server as empty. The
# second bug had not hit it: it was on Steam's current build, 26430253,
# installed on 2026-11-04 twelve minutes after Steam published it.
# Since 1.8.1 a failed player count makes an update or restart WAIT instead.
#
# Rollback 1, the dev-proton build this server ran from 2026-10-16:
#   mornedhels/enshrouded-server@sha256:d122801bb54498f41a6c0d8b27f336ec4c9266ffd5e4660611cb7c20c162318f
#
# Why not the Wine build this server started on: it ran, but with two players
# exploring it averaged 35-39 ms per world update and logged "Bad Performance"
# every 5 s - the in-game "high server load" warning - while the VM sat 77%
# idle. That Wine build does all thread synchronisation through one wineserver
# process; Proton does it in the kernel (fsync). Side by side on copies of the
# same world, idle: 4.3 ms -> 1.8 ms per update. See README.md, "The image".
#
# Rollback 2 (it works, but lags with players on) is the 1.7.2-wine digest:
#   mornedhels/enshrouded-server@sha256:6bd473b78e5331a0fc86553d9e9ddef5c712d7e9b356af385aa90e772f931019
ENSHROUDED_IMAGE=mornedhels/enshrouded-server@sha256:160d469d7a2dbed3a8dac2b1904df387302bfa0f524a26344582e1b76ca46fe4

# Host paths & runtime identity. DATA_DIR holds gitignored runtime state:
#   data/game  -> /opt/enshrouded   the ~8 GB game install, the world
#                                   (server/savegame) and the live config
#                                   (server/enshrouded_server.json)
#
# 4711 is the image's own default and deliberately NOT an account on the VM
# (the other games run as ubuntu, uid 1000, which has sudo). If something ever
# broke out of this container it would land as a uid that owns nothing here.
DATA_DIR=./data
PUID=4711
PGID=4711
TZ=UTC

# Enshrouded's ONE port. Since Content Update 2 there is no separate game port:
# play, Steam query and the server browser all use the query port.
GAME_PORT=15637
